PPT Outline: Building an Internal Data Tool with Gemini
Slide 1: Project Overview & Objectives
• The Goal: Centralize scattered Python scripts into a single, user-friendly web interface.
• Target Users: Global Internal Audit DA Team.
• Key Functionality: Input specific IDs \rightarrow Run Backend Python Logic \rightarrow Display Result \rightarrow Download as Excel.
Slide 2: Data & Logic Framework
• Dual Data Sources:
• QC Part2: Containing columns for ID, Test, and System.
• Network Table: Containing columns for Table Name and AE.
• Triple Logic Modules:
• Logic 1 (py1): Test Scenarios Extraction (Multi-ID filtering).
• Logic 2 (py2): Systems Extraction (Multi-ID filtering).
• Logic 3 (py3): DW Network Tool (Multi-AE filtering).
Slide 3: The Iterative Development Process
• Prompting Strategy: Started with "Dummy Data" and hand-drawn layout sketches to establish a Minimum Viable Product (MVP).
• Evolutionary Coding:
• Phase 1: Basic HTML/CSS/JS structure with Flask backend.
• Phase 2: Transitioned from dummy lists to real .xlsx file reading using pandas.
• Phase 3: Upgraded search logic from single-match to "Comma-Separated" multi-matching using .isin() logic.
Slide 4: Challenges & Solutions (The "Pivots")
• UI/UX Refinement: * Problem: Standard buttons looked generic.
• Solution: Reference-based styling with red accents (vertical bars) and Emojis for better visual hierarchy.
• The Overflow Problem: * Problem: Large datasets pushed the "Clear" and "Export" buttons off-screen.
• Solution: Implemented flex-shrink: 0 for sidebars and overflow: auto with min-width: 0 for the central canvas to ensure a "Frozen Pane" effect.
• Rendering Bottlenecks: * Problem: 10,000+ rows caused browser lag.
• Solution: Implemented a "Preview Mode" (Rendering top 100 rows) while maintaining full dataset integrity for the Export function.
Slide 5: The "Aha!" Moment with AI
• Zero to One: Built a full-stack application without manually writing boilerplate code.
• Contextual Debugging: Gemini acted as a senior architect to solve complex CSS Flexbox issues in real-time.
• Efficiency: Reduced development time from days to hours by focusing on "what to build" rather than "how to syntax."
Slide 6: The Road Ahead: Next Steps
• API Integration: Connect the backend to Large Language Model (LLM) APIs.
• Natural Language Querying: Allow users to ask "Show me all systems for Audit 123" instead of just typing IDs.
• Automated Insights: Use AI to summarize the "Extract" results and highlight anomalies automatically before the user even downloads the file.
